<title>JAPAN: Japan Dec zinc imports fall 48.5 pct yr/yr--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Dec zinc imports fall 48.5 pct yr/yr--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined zinc imports in December fell to 4,637 tonnes, down 48.5 percent from 9,003 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, Ministry of Finance data released on Monday showed.</p>
<p>Figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 Dec 96    Nov 96	Dec 95</p>
<p> Total		 4,637     3,324	 9,003</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> China		 2,050     1,044	 7,368</p>
<p>Refined zinc imports 1996 were 134,798 tonnes, up 15.2 percent from 116,986 tonnes the year before, reflecting the closure of two Japanese zinc refineries in the past two years.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
</text>
